## **IX. TOKENIZÁCIÓ ÉS LANGUAGE MODEL SPECIFICS**

### **1. Tokenizer/MGT.zig - Morpheme-aware Gradient Tokenizer**

Ez egy **nyelvészeti alapú tokenizer**, amely **morfémák** (nyelvtani egységek) szerint bont.

**Koncepció:**

Hagyományos tokenizerek (BPE, WordPiece):
- **Statisztikai** gyakoriság alapján
- Nem vesznek figyelembe **nyelvi struktúrát**

MGT:
- **Morfológiai analízis** (tőszó, képző, rag)
- **Gradiens alapú** (neurális hálózat tanítja a szegmentációt)

**Implementáció:**

```zig
pub const MGT = struct {
    vocab: std.StringHashMap(u32),
    reverse_vocab: std.AutoHashMap(u32, []const u8),
    morpheme_boundaries: NeuralBoundaryPredictor,
    allocator: Allocator,

    const NeuralBoundaryPredictor = struct {
        model: RSFLayer,

        pub fn predictBoundary(self: *NeuralBoundaryPredictor, context: []const u8) !f32 {
            // Convert character context to embedding
            var input = try Tensor.init(self.model.allocator, &.{context.len});
            defer input.deinit();

            for (context, 0..) |char, i| {
                input.data[i] = @as(f32, @floatFromInt(char)) / 255.0;
            }

            // Forward pass
            const output = try self.model.forward(&input);
            defer output.deinit();

            return output.data[0];  // Probability of boundary
        }
    };

    pub fn encode(self: *MGT, text: []const u8, output: *std.ArrayList(u32)) !void {
        var segments = std.ArrayList([]const u8).init(self.allocator);
        defer segments.deinit();

        // Step 1: Morpheme segmentation (neural-guided)
        var i: usize = 0;
        var segment_start: usize = 0;

        while (i < text.len) : (i += 1) {
            const context_start = if (i >= 5) i - 5 else 0;
            const context = text[context_start..i + 1];

            const boundary_prob = try self.morpheme_boundaries.predictBoundary(context);

            if (boundary_prob > 0.5 or i == text.len - 1) {
                // Create segment
                const segment = text[segment_start..i + 1];
                try segments.append(segment);
                segment_start = i + 1;
            }
        }

        // Step 2: Map segments to token IDs
        for (segments.items) |segment| {
            if (self.vocab.get(segment)) |token_id| {
                try output.append(token_id);
            } else {
                // Fallback: character-level encoding
                for (segment) |char| {
                    const char_key = &[_]u8{char};
                    const char_id = self.vocab.get(char_key) orelse 0;  // <UNK>
                    try output.append(char_id);
                }
            }
        }
    }

    pub fn decode(self: *MGT, tokens: []const u32, allocator: Allocator) ![]u8 {
        var result = std.ArrayList(u8).init(allocator);

        for (tokens) |token_id| {
            if (self.reverse_vocab.get(token_id)) |text| {
                try result.appendSlice(text);
            } else {
                // Unknown token
                try result.appendSlice("<UNK>");
            }
        }

        return result.toOwnedSlice();
    }
};
```

**Training (morpheme boundary predictor):**

```zig
pub fn trainBoundaryPredictor(
    mgt: *MGT,
    corpus: []const u8,
    labeled_boundaries: []const usize
) !void {
    const context_size = 5;

    for (labeled_boundaries) |boundary_pos| {
        if (boundary_pos < context_size) continue;

        // Positive example (boundary)
        const pos_context = corpus[boundary_pos - context_size .. boundary_pos + 1];
        var pos_input = try Tensor.init(mgt.allocator, &.{context_size + 1});
        defer pos_input.deinit();
        for (pos_context, 0..) |char, i| {
            pos_input.data[i] = @as(f32, @floatFromInt(char)) / 255.0;
        }

        // Target: 1.0 (boundary exists)
        var target_pos = try Tensor.init(mgt.allocator, &.{1});
        defer target_pos.deinit();
        target_pos.data[0] = 1.0;

        const pred_pos = try mgt.morpheme_boundaries.model.forward(&pos_input);
        defer pred_pos.deinit();

        const loss_pos = (pred_pos.data[0] - 1.0) * (pred_pos.data[0] - 1.0);
        try mgt.morpheme_boundaries.model.backward(&pred_pos, &target_pos);

        // Negative example (no boundary)
        const neg_pos = boundary_pos + 2;
        if (neg_pos + context_size >= corpus.len) continue;

        const neg_context = corpus[neg_pos - context_size .. neg_pos + 1];
        var neg_input = try Tensor.init(mgt.allocator, &.{context_size + 1});
        defer neg_input.deinit();
        for (neg_context, 0..) |char, i| {
            neg_input.data[i] = @as(f32, @floatFromInt(char)) / 255.0;
        }

        var target_neg = try Tensor.init(mgt.allocator, &.{1});
        defer target_neg.deinit();
        target_neg.data[0] = 0.0;

        const pred_neg = try mgt.morpheme_boundaries.model.forward(&neg_input);
        defer pred_neg.deinit();

        const loss_neg = (pred_neg.data[0] - 0.0) * (pred_neg.data[0] - 0.0);
        try mgt.morpheme_boundaries.model.backward(&pred_neg, &target_neg);
    }
}
```

**Előnyök:**

- **Nyelvtani konzisztencia** (pl. "unhappiness" = "un-" + "happy" + "-ness")
- **Jobb OOV kezelés** (out-of-vocabulary words)
- **Kisebb vocab** (morfémák < teljes szavak)

